The exact result depends on the firewall's configuration and rule-processing behavior. Some firewalls process rules in order and stop at the first match, while others use different mechanisms.

Why host-based firewalls matter: Even if a device connects to an untrusted network, its own firewall can restrict which connections are permitted to reach or leave that device.

A firewall is not a complete anti-malware solution. It controls network traffic; it does not automatically detect every malicious file or stop every attack.

4.3.6 Combining security controls

Security is stronger when different controls work together.

Consider a school laptop:

Control

	

Purpose




